Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:51:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] compartments: the revoked ledger gives back what it can
 and a refused mirror stops the apps only once it is written

Review A7 and A8. restoreLocation dropped an entry on any SecurityException, although only a gone package or a permission it no longer asks for should; the background permission was granted before the foreground ones and read after they were taken; a revoke with a full ledger is logged, and the permission is still taken (fail closed, the automated review of the commit flagged the first version that left it). A failed mirror write stopped the changed apps after 2 s, so they restarted with the old files and the retry 10 s later never stopped them again: the stops now wait in mPendingStop until a mirror pass succeeds.
---
 .../CompartmentsPolicyService.java            | 77 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 67 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/compartments/CompartmentsPolicyService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/compartments/CompartmentsPolicyService.java
